<LegalLayout title="Privacy Policy" updated="16 August 2026" description="Privacy Policy for the Aether platform, operated by Optim Enterprises B.V.">
  <p>
    This Privacy Policy explains how Optim Enterprises B.V. (“Aether”, “we”, “us”) collects, uses, and
    protects personal data when you use the Aether platform and related services (the “Service”). We
    are committed to data minimisation: Aether is designed so that subscriber network data can be
    processed at the edge rather than centralised.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Controller</h2>
  <p>
    The controller for personal data processed through the Service is Optim Enterprises B.V., a private
    limited company (besloten vennootschap) incorporated in the Netherlands, Chamber of Commerce number
    70926638, registered office in Amsterdam, Netherlands. For any privacy request, contact us at
    info@aether-io.com.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Data we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Account data — name, email address, organisation, and login credentials.</li>
    <li>Billing contact data — the billing name, email, and country used at checkout. Card and payment details are collected and processed directly by our payment provider; we do not store full card numbers.</li>
    <li>Service usage and telemetry — device and fleet metadata, configuration, event logs, and diagnostic information needed to operate the Service.</li>
    <li>Support communications — the content of messages you send us for support or enquiries.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. Purposes and legal bases</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To provide and operate the Service and your account — legal basis: performance of a contract.</li>
    <li>To process payments, invoicing, and taxes — legal basis: performance of a contract and compliance with a legal obligation.</li>
    <li>To secure, maintain, and improve the Service and prevent abuse — legal basis: our legitimate interests.</li>
    <li>To communicate with you about the Service, including service and billing notices — legal basis: contract and legitimate interests.</li>
    <li>To comply with legal and regulatory obligations — legal basis: legal obligation.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. Sub-processors</h2>
  <p>
    We use a limited set of trusted third parties to process personal data on our behalf, under
    appropriate data-processing terms:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Paddle (Paddle.com Market Ltd) — our Merchant of Record and payment processor. Paddle processes billing and payment personal data to take payment, calculate and remit taxes, and issue invoices.</li>
    <li>Airwallex — our financial services provider, used to receive and reconcile payouts and settlements.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Each provider processes personal data only as needed for its function. We will update this list if
    our sub-processors change.
  </p>

  <h2>5. International transfers</h2>
  <p>
    Some sub-processors may process data outside the European Economic Area. Where they do, the
    transfer is protected by an appropriate safeguard, such as an adequacy decision or the European
    Commission’s Standard Contractual Clauses.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Retention</h2>
  <p>
    We keep personal data only as long as needed for the purposes described above, or as required to
    meet legal, accounting, or reporting obligations. Billing and tax records are retained for the
    period required by law. When data is no longer needed, we delete or anonymise it.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Your rights</h2>
  <p>Subject to applicable law, you have the right to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>access the personal data we hold about you;</li>
    <li>request correction of inaccurate data;</li>
    <li>request erasure of your data;</li>
    <li>restrict or object to certain processing;</li>
    <li>receive your data in a portable format;</li>
    <li>withdraw consent where processing is based on consent.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    To exercise any right, email info@aether-io.com. You also have the right to lodge a complaint with
    your local data-protection authority; in the Netherlands this is the Autoriteit Persoonsgegevens.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Security</h2>
  <p>
    We apply technical and organisational measures appropriate to the risk, including encryption in
    transit, access controls, and audit logging, to protect personal data against unauthorised access,
    loss, or misuse.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    The Service uses only cookies and similar technologies that are strictly necessary to operate it,
    such as maintaining your authenticated session. We do not use third-party advertising or cross-site
    tracking cookies.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Children</h2>
  <p>
    The Service is intended for use by adults administering their own network or an organisation’s
    network. It is not directed to children, and we do not knowingly collect personal data from
    children.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Material changes will be communicated through
    the Service or by email, and the “last updated” date above will be revised.
  </p>

  <h2>12. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    For privacy questions or requests, contact <a href="mailto:info@aether-io.com">info@aether-io.com</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
